1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,740
Procrastination is often seen as the enemy of productivity.
拖延症常被视为生产力的大敌。

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:12,130
Images of lazy people with feet up on desks or wasting time to dodge work spring to mind at the very mention of the word.
一提到这个词，人们脑海里就会浮现出懒人把脚翘在桌上、或是为逃避工作而消磨时间的画面。

3
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:17,310
And there are many things which indicate that procrastination is a problem which needs addressing.
而且有诸多现象表明，拖延症是一个亟待解决的问题。

4
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:21,280
But could there be some benefits to it too?
但它难道就没有任何益处吗？

5
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:28,730
We live in a high-octane world – always on the go, racing from one task to another.
我们生活在一个快节奏的世界里，总是行色匆匆，忙完一项任务紧跟着就开始下一项任务。

6
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:36,610
And at times, duties, be it work or personal, can feel relentless – with our nose constantly to the grindstone.
有时候，无论是工作还是私人事务，这些职责都显得永无止境，让我们不得不埋头苦干。

7
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:40,680
Sometimes we just need to switch off, chill out and reboot.
有时候，我们就是需要彻底放松、舒缓身心、重新调整状态。

8
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:45,420
A little procrastination can help detach us from the pressures of modern life.
适度的拖延，能帮我们暂时摆脱现代生活的压力。

9
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:53,990
According to psychotherapist F Diane Barth, watching TV, taking a long bath or listening to music can help us to ease off.
心理治疗师F·黛安·巴特表示，看电视、泡个热水澡或是听听音乐，都能帮助我们放松下来。

10
00:00:53,990 --> 00:00:58,480
And it’s possible that procrastination has become more prevalent during the pandemic.
在疫情期间，拖延症的现象可能变得更为普遍。

11
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:09,660
With many countries going through lockdowns, some of us have suddenly found ourselves with more time – not having the hours of commutes, or options of social activities we once took for granted.
随着许多国家实施封锁政策，我们中的一些人突然拥有了更多空闲时间——那些曾经习以为常的通勤时间没了，各类社交活动的选择也消失了。

12
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:17,380
Being at home, many of us quickly discovered that it is impossible to be productive 24-7.
居家生活让很多人很快意识到，想要一天24小时、一周7天时刻保持高效是不可能的。

13
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:26,020
That extra relaxation can help us to be more productive or creative in the long run, allowing us to clear our minds and focus better.
从长远来看，这些额外的放松时间能让我们更具效率和创造力，帮助我们理清思绪、更好地集中注意力。

14
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:31,390
The issue is that many of us see that time not working as lost time.
问题在于，我们很多人都把不工作的时间看作是虚度光阴。

15
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:36,880
And we almost develop a sense of guilt related to not making the most of every moment.
而且我们还会因为没能充分利用每一刻而产生愧疚感。

16
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:49,030
German sociologist and economist Max Weber says that we’ve almost got to the point of believing that the busier we are, the better, and that there is a sense of morality connected with time usage.
德国社会学家兼经济学家马克斯·韦伯表示，我们几乎已经陷入了一种认知误区，认为越忙碌越好，并且将时间的利用方式和道德感挂钩。

17
00:01:49,030 --> 00:01:55,690
It seems important to remember that taking a little time away from yourself is not just slacking off.
但我们必须记住，给自己留一点放松的时间，绝不仅仅是偷懒。

18
00:01:55,690 --> 00:02:05,020
So, while being productive is important, it seems that some amount of downtime and procrastination can help us to relax and become more focussed.
因此，尽管保持高效很重要，但适度的休息和拖延，似乎能帮助我们放松身心、提升专注力。

19
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:11,120
The next time you feel really stressed, why not try wasting a little time? You might just like it.
下次当你感到压力山大时，不妨试着“浪费”一点时间，说不定你会喜欢这种感觉。
